WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
Watch this woman. She's warning her audience not to drink bottled water.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:12.740
She's an Amish grandmother. She has more than 350,000 followers. She's also entirely AI

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:21.540
generated. Her name is Melonskia. She's selling a $50 supplement called Modern Antidope. Untested,

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:28.840
no clinical trial, and until the New York Times exposed the operation, her account had no AI

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:36.440
disclosure at all. It still doesn't, not really. Instagram added an automated label to recent posts.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:43.720
The same one applied to photos that have merely been retouched. Her bio still presents her as a

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:49.840
real person. This is what unregulated AI influencers look like. And the same playbook

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:55.860
just put real people in the hospital recently with different AI generated personas selling a

00:00:55.860 --> 00:01:01.980
different supplement. And there is no federal law stopping any of it. Full breakdown on Substack.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:02.920
Link is in my bio.
